  "description": "Holdout set: written after the rules and the prompt were finished, before any parser had been run on it, and not used to change either (the README says where that was broken and what it cost). Same instruments, prices and conventions as dev.json. Includes the two phrasings from the first live check of the models.",
  "conventions": [
    "Prices and quantities are display units, as a person writes them (BTC in coins).",
    "No price and no 'market' means a market order: the proposal says 'at market' and warns.",
    "timeInForce is only given when the text states it. Limit and stop-limit orders default to GTC; market and stop orders have none.",
    "A cancel names a symbol and side only if the text does; null means all.",
    "unclear: no quantity or a vague one, money instead of a quantity, two orders, an unknown instrument, a question or chat, invalid numbers (fractions of a share, off the tick, below the lot, zero, negative), contradictions, an iceberg with IOC/FOK.",
    "A buy with a stop loss below its price (or a sell with one above) is a bracket: an entry plus a protective exit, i.e. two orders, so unclear. A stop loss on its own with a sell is one order: a sell stop."
  ],
